    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Time-Bounded Constraint Relaxation with Compensatory Recovery Protocol: Temporarily relax FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.50 (from 0.40) and Noise ceiling to 82.0 dB (from 80.0 dB) for a defined production window not to exceed 5 consecutive working days. Mandatory compensatory measures must be documented and enforced: mandatory 48-hour low-intensity recovery rotation after the window, audiometric monitoring before and after, and written risk acceptance signed by the production manager and EHS officer. This option fully closes the demand gap but explicitly violates the spirit of human-centric constraints and must be treated as an exception requiring formal governance sign-off. Relaxed limits still fall within legal maximums in most jurisdictions but exceed the organisation's own protective thresholds.
