       Q: What is the exact shift duration in hours (e.g., 8 h vs. 12 h)? The fatigue model combines task load with elapsed time, so the 0.4 hard ceiling has very different implications: an 8-hour shift allows more intensive early-shift work before the ceiling binds, whereas a 12-hour shift may require a consistently lower sustained task-load rate throughout, potentially constraining throughput from the first hour onward.
