    4. operator_fatigue_index threshold vs. cycle-rate increases
       Q: If raising the production pace to improve efficiency would push the fatigue index from a typical mid-shift value (~0.30) toward the 0.40 hard limit, is there a maximum allowable pace step-up per interval (e.g., no more than +10% cycle rate per 30 minutes) to prevent a sudden, hard-to-reverse fatigue spike?
       A: Cap any single cycle-rate increase at +15% of the current rate per 30-minute window and reproject the fatigue trajectory before authorising each subsequent step-up.
    5. ambient_noise_level measurement averaging period
       Q: Is the 80 dB(A) limit enforced as a full-shift LAeq average, or must every shorter sub-interval (e.g., any rolling 15-minute window) also stay below 80 dB? A shift-long average can conceal peaks that create hearing-damage risk even when the daily average appears compliant.
